  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Which of the following vitamin is helpful in the blood clotting?</p>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "Vitamin <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Vitamin <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Vitamin <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "Vitamin <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Vitamin helpful in the blood clotting is Vitamin <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>.</p><p>Vitamin K is a fat soluble vitamin&nbsp;required for normal blood clotting. Its deficiency leads to slow or delayed blood clotting and&nbsp;haemorrhage (blood loss). Vitamin K is&nbsp;required for synthesis of prothrombin in the liver&nbsp;where the vitamin K-dependent carboxylation in prothrombin synthesis occurs.</p><p>Note: Question has been&nbsp;slightly modified for its correctness.</p>"
  }
